WEBVTT

00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:15,470
Dr. Cutters, I'm 67, your old female. I was diagnosed with an enlarged bladder. I have no pain.

00:00:15,470 --> 00:00:20,910
They did diagnostic testing and just determined I do not have your

00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:27,870
retention. They told me I must have had your retention in the past. My bladder

00:00:27,870 --> 00:00:32,150
size is greater than 1,000 milliliters. I went to an alternative doctor and he

00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:38,070
suggested it was estrogen dominance. He wants me to apply table spoon of

00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:46,230
progestE, a brand name. Every night for two weeks out of the month. The theory is

00:00:46,230 --> 00:00:51,190
that if I apply it every day of the month, my liver will start canceling it out.

00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:57,510
What do you think and what would you do in my case? I take thyroid meds but I'm

00:00:57,510 --> 00:01:04,830
otherwise healthy. So I don't know if this alternative doctor is just following

00:01:04,830 --> 00:01:09,110
a protocol that they've used in the past that they've had success within the

00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:15,430
past. I do know that in order to find out if you have estrogen dominance, you

00:01:15,430 --> 00:01:22,710
should test. A Dutch test is probably the best test on the market right now. Dutch

00:01:22,710 --> 00:01:30,930
test is a dry urine hormone test and they test for all the estrogen. The

00:01:30,930 --> 00:01:36,210
metabolites in progesterone and antigen metabolites as well. You can see if you

00:01:36,210 --> 00:01:41,490
have estrogen dominance or not. I also test for cortisol levels. So ordering the

00:01:41,490 --> 00:01:47,610
Dutch test I think would be the right thing to do. So and then you'll know, is there

00:01:47,610 --> 00:01:53,250
any harm in taking progesterone? That's what that product I believe is. It's a

00:01:53,250 --> 00:02:00,090
topical progesterone. Is there any harm in taking that? Probably not. So if you have

00:02:00,090 --> 00:02:05,250
confidence in that doctor in the way that that doctor here she tested her, I don't

00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:12,810
think that there's necessarily any harm in doing that. With somebody your age, most

00:02:12,810 --> 00:02:19,410
people have low progesterone at 67 years old. I don't think there's harm in doing

00:02:19,410 --> 00:02:25,490
that. But I do think it's wise to get tested. So if that doctor will test, you can order

00:02:25,490 --> 00:02:29,730
test. If you're a course member, I don't know if this person is one of our

00:02:29,730 --> 00:02:34,690
course members. But if you are on our chronic disease autoimmune course or any of

00:02:34,690 --> 00:02:42,370
our other courses, you can run labs through them and it would be the Dutch

00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:46,530
complete test that I would record.

